1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
TEN (ENVELOPE)

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,000
[narrator] Ten:

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,000
The ability to envelop your body
in a shroud of Nen aura,

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
making it tougher and slowing
the effects of aging.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
ZETSU (SUPPRESS)

6
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Zetsu:

7
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
A technique which shuts off
your flow of Nen-aura.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Effective for concealing your presence
and recovering from fatigue.

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,000
REN (REFINE)

10
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Ren: A technique for creating
an especially strong Nen aura.

11
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
It is crucial for increasing your power.

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:28,000
HATSU (RELEASE)

13
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Hatsu:

14
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
The release of your Nen aura,
after using Ren to boost it.

15
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
These four elements
are known as the Four Exercises

16
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
and are critical to the mastery of Nen.

17
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,000
FOUR EXERCISES

18
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,000
[theme song playing]

19
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,000
You see my double is no mere illusion.

20
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:09,000
It’s real.

21
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Just as real as I am
until I make it vanish.

22
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,000
You must know this.

23
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,000
You felt it strike against you.

24
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,000
To put it simply

25
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,000
you are going to have to
face two of me at once!

26
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Now behold the culmination
of my mastery of Nen.

27
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,000
The True Tiger Bite Fist!

28
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:35,000
A x SURPRISING x WIN

29
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,000
[narrator] Kastro used Nen
to create a double of himself.

30
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,000
And his special attack -
the True Tiger Bite Fist

31
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
has severed Hisoka’s right arm.

32
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Which of these contenders
will emerge victorious?

33
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,000
[smirks]

34
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:02,000
[grunts]

35
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,000
[Cocco] Now what?!

36
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Hisoka has covered his right arm
with a scarf?

37
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Shall I demonstrate
my powers of clairvoyance?

38
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
[grumbles]

39
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,000
[Cocco] Wow!

40
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Wow! His right arm disappeared

41
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,000
and now cards are raining down!

42
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:29,000
What is he doing?!

43
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,000
[Hisoka]
The cards you see go from one to thirteen.

44
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
I want you to pick a number

45
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,000
and visualize that card in your head.

46
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
He’s doing a ‘pick a number’ trick?

47
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,000
[Hisoka] Ready?

48
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Once you’ve selected your number,

49
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
I want you to add four to it,

50
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,000
and then double the resulting sum.

51
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
After that subtract six and divide by two.

52
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Lastly, subtract your original number.

53
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Now, what do you get?

54
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,000
Gimme a sec…

55
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Did… he say subtract six?

56
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Ahh! I forgot already!

57
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,000
I knew your answer
even before you arrived at it yourself.

58
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,000
[audience gasping in shock]

59
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,000
The number you chose…

60
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
was one.

61
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,000
He’s totally right; it was!

62
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,000
How did he know?

63
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Really?!

64
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,000
[Cocco] What?! He’s insane!

65
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:40,000
This is the devil’s magic!

66
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,000
And he’s incorporated his own injury
into the trick!

67
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,000
I don’t get it.

68
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Why is he so calm?

69
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,000
There are no points for tricks.

70
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
It doesn’t have anything to do
with the match.

71
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,000
But still, he’s performing magic!

72
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,000
That’s the bizarre behavior
we expect from Hisoka!

73
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Would you like a souvenir?

74
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,000
You fool!

75
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,000
I will sever your left arm,

76
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:07,000
so that you’ll never be able
to mock anyone again!

77
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,000
You must not have heard me.

78
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,000
You can take it.

79
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,000
I’ll be more than happy to oblige!

80
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,000
[Cocco] Whoa! One of the Kastros
is charging forward!

81
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
[Kastro roaring]

82
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,000
[Cocco] This is unbelievable!

83
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:26,000
Hisoka has actually sacrificed
his remaining arm!

84
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,000
What in the world is this guy thinking?!

85
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,000
Wait, what?!

86
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:39,000
So, you did attack with your double.
How interesting.

87
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:41,000
If you had come at me yourself,

88
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,000
I was fully prepared to counterattack…

89
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,000
by using this.

90
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,000
[audience murmurs]

91
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:53,000
[Cocco] What? His severed right arm
is back together again!

92
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,000
But how?

93
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,000
[chuckling]

94
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,000
It’s another magic trick.

95
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Can you guess the secret behind this one?

96
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,000
He’s lying.

97
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:07,000
It’s obvious he’s using Nen
to accomplish this feat.

98
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,000
But... what kind of ability is this?

99
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,000
[Hisoka chuckles]

100
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,000
[Hisoka] What's wrong?

101
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,000
Are you scared?

102
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,000
You’re surprised
because you don’t know the trick.

103
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,000
But that’s magic.

104
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:27,000
See your power to create a double
is magnificent.

105
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,000
But now I understand how it’s done.

106
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:31,000
[grumbles]

107
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:34,000
[Hisoka] I can anticipate
how you’ll attack with your double.

108
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Not to mention,

109
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,000
I know how I should respond.

110
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
It’s too bad, really.

111
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:45,000
You had the potential
to become a skilled opponent...

112
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,000
and that’s why I decided to let you live.

113
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,000
I predict...

114
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:56,000
you’re going to dance yourself to death.

115
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,000
[growling]

116
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:01,000
[shouts] Shut up!

117
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,000
No! How did he pick me out?

118
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Doubles are made

119
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:12,000
from the image the original has in mind,

120
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:15,000
which is why they tend to be pristine.

121
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:19,000
But you can’t reproduce the grime
that builds up during combat.

122
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:22,000
Oh…

123
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:25,000
Had you not realized that yet?

124
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,000
[roaring]

125
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,000
[groans]

126
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,000
[Cocco] What is going on here?

127
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:45,000
I’m seeing it,
but I can’t even begin to understand it!

128
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:48,000
Is this another one
of Hisoka’s magic tricks?

129
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,000
Don't bother.

130
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
I hit you square in the lower jaw,

131
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,000
so you’ll be stunned for a minute or two.

132
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,000
[dazzled groaning]

133
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:59,000
And that means you’ll be helpless
to avoid my next attack.

134
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,000
What?!

135
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,000
Where did this attack come from?

136
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,000
I don’t have time for this.

137
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
I have to produce my double
to block the cards!

138
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:13,000
You can’t make another double.

139
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,000
Creating a new double using Nen

140
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:20,000
requires intense focus.

141
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,000
The only reason you were able
to produce and release them freely

142
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,000
was that up until now...

143
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,000
you were in a normal state of mind.

144
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:37,000
Using Nen to replicate
and manipulate something

145
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:41,000
that’s as complex as the human body,

146
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,000
is extremely difficult.

147
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,000
How difficult, you ask?

148
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:50,000
By the time you’ve learned
to use a double,

149
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:53,000
you’ve forgotten how to use Nen
for anything else.

150
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,000
Sad, really.

151
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:59,000
It’s a little something
I like to call “memory overload”.

152
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
You only lost because...

153
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,000
you squandered your memory capacity.

154
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:10,000
[cheering]

155
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
[Cocco]
Kastro’s down and he’s not getting up!

156
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,000
Hisoka wins by knockout!

157
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,000
Hisoka…

158
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
[cheering]

159
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,000
[Machi] Nice job.

160
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Well? Hurry up and show me your injuries.

161
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:52,000
I was never quite sure before

162
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:54,000
but today’s match proved it to me.

163
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Hm?

164
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,000
[Machi] You are an idiot.

165
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,000
That’s quite possible.

166
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Why did you decide
to put yourself in danger this way?

167
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,000
What was that?

168
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Performance art or something?

169
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,000
Well…

170
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:15,000
Okay. You’re paying me,
so I guess I can’t complain.

171
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
First, I’ll need to stop the bleeding.

172
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,000
[Hisoka] Hey…

173
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Be gentle, if you don’t mind.

174
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,000
Yeah, whatever.

175
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,000
Turn off your aura.

176
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,000
[smirks]

177
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:49,000
[Machi] I’ll start with your left arm.

178
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,000
Here we go.

179
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:57,000
Starting Nen Stitches.

180
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:58,000
NEN STITCHES

181
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,000
There. All done.

182
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:12,000
Bones and blood vessels,
nerves, and muscles.

183
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
They’re basically all connected, now.

184
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Ahh! That’s brilliant.

185
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,000
[Machi] Next…

186
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,000
I’ll do your right arm.

187
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,000
You can hold it yourself this time.

188
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,000
[Hisoka impressed] Mm.

189
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:37,000
This is always so fascinating to watch.

190
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:44,000
I so enjoy getting to see
your Nen stitches in action

191
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:47,000
that maybe I injured myself on purpose.

192
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,000
Fine, whatever.

193
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:51,000
Twenty mil for the left one,
fifty for the right one.

194
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:52,000
All right?

195
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
Now. Fork it over.

196
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:57,000
I’ll transfer it
directly into your account.

197
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,000
All right.

198
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:01,000
And you can treat
the rest of the injuries yourself.

199
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,000
[Hisoka]
Your bedside manner could be better.

200
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:07,000
You should be able to manage
with your Bungee Gum...

201
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,000
and your Texture Surprise.

202
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Ah.

203
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,000
I guess I should conceal them.

204
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,000
If I do...

205
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:18,000
they’ll think my arms
were healed magically during the match.

206
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:24,000
This is nothing more
than an ordinary scarf.

207
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,000
I use Bungee Gum

208
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,000
to attach it to my arm,

209
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:33,000
then Texture Surprise
to create a layer of skin.

210
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,000
[Machi] He’s so fast.

211
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,000
Fast enough to fool a Nen master

212
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,000
into believing
the arm had actually healed

213
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
before he thought to take a second look.

214
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,000
Next, I’ll do the left.

215
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Bungee Gum.

216
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,000
ELASTIC LOVE
BUNGEE GUM

217
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:53,000
He modifies his aura,

218
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:56,000
making it both elastic and sticky.

219
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,000
It stretches extremely well,

220
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,000
contracts swiftly when needed,

221
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
adheres to most substances

222
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,000
and it can be removed at any time.

223
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:08,000
Oh, by the way
I call this trick ‘Bungee Gum’

224
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:10,000
because that was the name
of my favorite chewing gum

225
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,000
when I was a child.

226
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Yeah, you really didn’t need
to tell me all that.

227
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Texture Surprise.

228
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:21,000
He combines his aura with imagery

229
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:24,000
in order to reproduce
the appearance of skin.

230
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,000
FLIMSY LIES
TEXTURE SURPRISE

231
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
It’s essentially a high-quality copy,

232
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:30,000
so you can tell it’s fake
if you actually touch it.

233
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:33,000
But Hisoka probably finds
that drawback exciting.

234
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,000
I call this one Texture Surprise

235
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,000
which comes from the gag stickers

236
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:41,000
that were included with a popular snack
not too long ago.

237
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:45,000
Like I said,
I really didn’t need to know all that.

238
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Weren’t you impressed

239
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,000
by my application of these abilities
during the match?

240
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:52,000
I was almost certain you were.

241
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,000
[Machi] Huh?!

242
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:56,000
Well, you did see everything, didn’t you?

243
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Yeah… I think I did…

244
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,000
You started with a misdirection,

245
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:05,000
tossing 13 cards into the air.

246
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:07,000
At the same time you threw your arm,

247
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,000
attaching it to the roof with Bungee Gum

248
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:13,000
and the scarf to the ground the same way.

249
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:16,000
But you didn’t let go.

250
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:19,000
The aura from each was connected
to the stump of your right arm.

251
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,000
And that’s not all.

252
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:26,000
The cards you threw as a distraction
were also secured to the ground

253
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:30,000
with the ends of the 13 strands of aura
connected to your left hand.

254
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,000
And then,

255
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,000
when you threw the ace of spades
at Kastro…

256
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,000
Would you like a souvenir?

257
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:41,000
Cocco]
… the aura in your left hand was released.

258
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:43,000
They connected.

259
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:47,000
All 13 of the aura strands
you had been holding,

260
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,000
stuck to Kastro’s body.

261
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:50,000
Correct.

262
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:53,000
You’re much more observant
than Kastro was.

263
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
[Machi] I also noticed

264
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:58,000
that you employed one
of the basic techniques of Nen Zetsu -

265
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:00,000
to help make your aura almost invisible.

266
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,000
Yes. However, there was one weakness.

267
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:05,000
[Machi] Yeah.

268
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,000
Pretty much anybody who’s learned Ren,

269
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:09,000
another basic Nen technique,

270
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,000
could have detected it easily…

271
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:14,000
by focusing the aura in their eyes
and watching.

272
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:20,000
That’s why you used
that crazy magic trick of yours

273
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
to throw him off guard
while you just stood there,

274
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:25,000
smiling and pretending to be nonchalant.

275
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:28,000
It even worked as a kind of camouflage.

276
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,000
You had him convinced
that your lack of aura

277
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:32,000
was a sign of confidence.

278
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,000
Once you were satisfied

279
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,000
that everything
was going according to plan,

280
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:40,000
you surreptitiously extended a thread
of aura from your left hand,

281
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,000
the one holding the cards

282
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:45,000
and connected it directly
to Kastro’s chin.

283
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:47,000
Everything was ready.

284
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,000
You’d already used Texture Surprise

285
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:54,000
to alter the scarf on the floor
to resemble human skin.

286
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,000
And so,

287
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:59,000
when Kastro attacked your left arm,

288
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,000
you activated the Bungee Gum

289
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
between your right arm
and the scarf on the floor.

290
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Your arm was restored

291
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,000
and the scarf concealed the wound,

292
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,000
leaving everyone convinced
your right arm

293
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:11,000
was magically back.

294
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:16,000
However, this performance
had the unfortunate effect

295
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:18,000
of bringing Kastro back to his senses.

296
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:22,000
It made no sense for a severed arm
to simply reappear,

297
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,000
especially in pristine condition.

298
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,000
It was then that Kastro realized

299
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,000
I was actually using Nen
to accomplish these feats

300
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:32,000
and not magic,
as he was led to believe.

301
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,000
That’s true.

302
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,000
But you didn’t miss
the ever-so-subtle change

303
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:37,000
in his psychological condition.

304
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:42,000
See your power to create a double
is magnificent.

305
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,000
But now I understand how it’s done.

306
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,000
[grumbles]

307
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:48,000
[Hisoka] I can anticipate
how you’ll attack with your double.

308
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,000
Not to mention,

309
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,000
I know how I should respond.

310
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:55,000
It’s too bad, really.

311
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:59,000
You had the potential
to become a skilled opponent...

312
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:04,000
and that’s why I decided to let you live.

313
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,000
[grumbles]

314
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:09,000
[Machi]
You saw that Kastro was about to recover.

315
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
I predict...

316
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:14,000
you’re going to dance yourself to death.

317
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,000
[Machi]
But then you pushed him over the edge.

318
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:22,000
[shouts] Shut up!

319
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,000
No! How did he pick me out?

320
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,000
You can’t reproduce the grime

321
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:29,000
that builds up during combat.

322
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,000
[Machi] And just like that,

323
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:38,000
you were able to expose
the weakness of his doubles.

324
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,000
But if he had just stayed
calm and composed,

325
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:43,000
then he actually
would have had a fighting chance.

326
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,000
However...

327
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:47,000
Kastro couldn't bear the mental strain.

328
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:53,000
[roaring]

329
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,000
And so... he lost.

330
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:04,000
You do realize

331
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
just how perfect both of those abilities
are for someone like you, don’t you?

332
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:09,000
They’re practically tailor-made.

333
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:12,000
As opposed to Kastro’s double ability,

334
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
my techniques are so adaptable

335
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:17,000
that they don’t lose their effectiveness,
if my opponent knows about them.

336
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,000
[Machi] Well...

337
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:23,000
I’m heading back now.

338
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:24,000
Already?

339
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,000
Yeah, why stick around
after the job is done?

340
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,000
There’s only so much
that Nen Stitches can do,

341
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:34,000
so try not to overdo it
until your arm is firmly attached.

342
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Oh, right...

343
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,000
I came here for a reason.

344
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,000
Hm?

345
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:42,000
[Machi] The message has been changed.

346
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,000
All Troupe members
are to be in York New City

347
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,000
by noon, August 30th,

348
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,000
not just those
who don’t have anything better to do.

349
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,000
[Hisoka] Will the boss be coming?

350
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,000
[Machi] Probably.

351
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:57,000
This could turn out
to be our biggest mission yet.

352
00:18:58,000 --> 00:18:59,000
So, know if you blow it off,

353
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,000
the boss might hunt you down himself.

354
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:04,000
Now that is scary.

355
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Oh, by the way…

356
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:08,000
-Care to join me for dinner tonight?
-[door closes]

357
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:12,000
What a pity.

358
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,000
-[gasps]
-[door opens]

359
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Killua! So how was Hisoka’s fight?
Tell me!

360
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:26,000
Boring. Don’t worry,
you didn’t miss much.

361
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,000
Boring?

362
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,000
And Hisoka? Did he win?

363
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Okay, I was lying.

364
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:40,000
Huh?

365
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:43,000
[Killua] It was an incredible fight.

366
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:45,000
Hate to say it

367
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:48,000
but I watched Hisoka win
and I still don’t know how.

368
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,000
You seriously couldn’t tell how he did it?

369
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,000
Gon.

370
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,000
You and me…

371
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:58,000
we’ve got to learn all that we can
about Nen.

372
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Yeah!

373
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,000
[Machi] He’s such a mystery.

374
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,000
He never talks about his past.

375
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:28,000
It doesn’t interest him.

376
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:34,000
He’ll probably forget
what Kastro looks like by tomorrow.

377
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:39,000
He doesn’t belong to anything or anyone.

378
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:44,000
He’s his own man,
no doubt about it.

379
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:49,000
Because he’s absolutely convinced
that he’s the most powerful.

380
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,000
[tap squeaks]

381
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:01,000
[wet feet slapping on the floor]

382
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:02,000
Hmm...

383
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:05,000
Oh, I forgot to take... this off.

384
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:11,000
A spider?

385
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:16,000
I found some new toys to play with.

386
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:20,000
Time to start the hunt.

387
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:34,000
[narrator] Hisoka has been masquerading
as a member of the Phantom Troupe.

388
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,000
But to him,

389
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:39,000
the Phantom Troupe
is nothing more than another target.

390
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:46,000
[theme song playing]

391
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:53,000
[Gon] Coming up:

392
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:55,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

393
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:56,000
[both] ...Hunterpedia!

394
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:58,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

395
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:59,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

396
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:02,000
Today we meet Kastro,
who uses the Tiger Bite Fist.

397
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:04,000
He makes a double of himself with Nen.

398
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Those aren’t easy to deal with!

399
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:09,000
With this double,
I can use the True Tiger Bite Fist!

400
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:10,000
[both] Scary, isn’t it?

401
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:15,000
Next time:

402
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:17,000
An x Empty x Threat.

403
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,000
Achoo!

404
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:19,000
Do I have a cold?

405
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,000
[Killua] I bet someone's talking about you
behind your back.

406
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:23,000
[Gon] Aunt Mito?
